        "original_id": "b78f64cf-cdba-5ffd-9f4a-e194358a0fcb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fairview, Kentucky; Christian County; Todd County; Kentucky\n- People: Jefferson Davis; Franklin Pierce\n- Roles: President of the Confederate States of America; United States Secretary of War\n- Sites: Jefferson Davis State Historic Site\n\nFacts:\n- Fairview is a small census-designated place on the boundary between Christian County and Todd County in western Kentucky.\n- Jefferson Davis was born in Fairview, Kentucky.\n- Jefferson Davis later became President of the Confederate States of America.\n- The Jefferson Davis State Historic Site is located in Fairview, Kentucky.\n- Jefferson Davis served as the 23rd United States Secretary of War from 1853 to 1857.\n- Jefferson Davis served as United States Secretary of War under President Franklin Pierce.",
